# This file is a TEMPLATE. It is committed to git on purpose and must never
# contain a real value. Copy it to `.env` and put the real values there:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is listed in .gitignore, so it stays on your computer and is never
# uploaded. On Vercel or Netlify you paste the same values into the hosting
# dashboard instead of uploading a file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The site needs NOTHING here right now. It is a static site: checkout links
# are public URLs and live in src/config/offers.ts, not here. Anything in this
# file would be baked into the public HTML anyway.
#
# A secret key belongs here ONLY if something runs on a server. If a service
# ever hands you a key labelled "secret" or "private", it goes in .env — never
# in src/, never in a component, never in a screenshot.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Example of the shape, kept commented out so nothing is switched on by accident.
# Anything prefixed PUBLIC_ is visible to visitors — never put a secret behind it.
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=
